# Word of a newer release (ui/UpdateCheck.h): the main menu's first row and
# about:sashfold say it, and say nothing while there is none. Nothing is
# downloaded: the row leads to the release's page.
resize 900 600
open about:sashfold
assert-text Version
assert-no-text is out
assert-text The daily check for a newer version is off.
main-menu
assert-menu New tab | New container tab > | - | Find in page | (Reader mode) | Bookmarks > | - | Themes > | Command palette | - | Developer tools | (View page source) | - | About Sashfold | Quit
main-menu
assert-menus 0

# The check is on and knows of nothing newer: the page says how it asks.
newer-release
reload
assert-no-text is out
assert-text Once a day Sashfold asks its releases page
main-menu
assert-menu New tab | New container tab > | - | Find in page | (Reader mode) | Bookmarks > | - | Themes > | Command palette | - | Developer tools | (View page source) | - | About Sashfold | Quit
main-menu

# It was told of one: the menu's first row, set off from the rest, and a
# box on the page with the way to it.
newer-release 0.9.9
main-menu
assert-menu Sashfold 0.9.9 is out | - | New tab | New container tab > | - | Find in page | (Reader mode) | Bookmarks > | - | Themes > | Command palette | - | Developer tools | (View page source) | - | About Sashfold | Quit
assert-golden goldens/update-notice-menu.png
main-menu
reload
assert-text Sashfold 0.9.9 is out.
assert-text What changed, and where to get it
assert-text downloaded or replaced on its own.
assert-golden goldens/update-notice-about.png

# And it goes when there is none any more (the build caught up).
newer-release
reload
assert-no-text is out
main-menu
assert-menu New tab | New container tab > | - | Find in page | (Reader mode) | Bookmarks > | - | Themes > | Command palette | - | Developer tools | (View page source) | - | About Sashfold | Quit
